---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout title="Ayush Mishra | Computer Scientist & AI Researcher">
  <!-- Bio Section with Floated Round Portrait (Chip Huyen style) -->
  <section id="about" class="intro-bio">
    <div class="profile-container">
      <a href="https://github.com/ayush190511" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="profile-img-link" title="Ayush Mishra">
        <img src="/assets/logo2.jpeg" alt="Ayush Mishra" class="profile-img" />
      </a>
      <div class="profile-pill-badge">
        <span class="status-dot"></span>
        <span>Bengaluru, India</span>
      </div>
    </div>

    <p>
      I’m <strong>Ayush Mishra</strong>, a Computer Scientist and AI Researcher based in Bengaluru, India. I specialize in <strong>Multimodal Deep Learning</strong>, <strong>Vision Transformers</strong>, and <strong>high-performance ML systems</strong>.
    </p>

    <p>
      Currently, I serve as an <strong>Academic Researcher &amp; Faculty Mentor</strong> in the Department of Information Science and Engineering at <a href="https://www.dsce.edu.in/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"><strong>Dayananda Sagar College of Engineering (DSCE), Bengaluru</strong></a>, where I mentor engineering students in Deep Learning architectures and guide applied research initiatives.
    </p>

    <p>
      I completed my <strong>M.Tech in Computer Science and Engineering (Data Science)</strong> from the prestigious <a href="https://www.svnit.ac.in/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"><strong>Sardar Vallabhbhai National Institute of Technology (SVNIT), Surat</strong></a> (CGPA 8.42/10). My master’s research culminated in a peer-reviewed paper accepted and presented at the <em>International Conference on Intelligent Computing, Cognitive Networks, and Smart Systems</em> (<a href="/research"><strong>IC2NS2</strong></a>, Tentative Publication: December 2026), introducing a novel Cross-Modal Gated Fusion framework that achieved <strong>96.66% SOTA accuracy</strong> on the benchmark SPECTRA dataset.
    </p>

    <p>
      I also build high-throughput tools and platforms. Some of them include <a href="https://allagecalculator.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"><strong>AllAgeCalculator.com</strong></a> (a zero-latency chronological analytics engine), automated end-to-end MLOps disease classification pipelines (DVC, MLflow, Docker, AWS), and real-time customer churn prediction microservices with sub-50ms inference and SHAP explainability.
    </p>

    <p>
      You can find my code on <a href="https://github.com/ayush190511" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"><strong>GitHub</strong></a>, connect on <a href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/ayush190511/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"><strong>LinkedIn</strong></a>, track my competitive benchmarks on <a href="https://www.kaggle.com/ayush190511" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"><strong>Kaggle</strong></a>, or view my citations on <a href="https://scholar.google.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"><strong>Google Scholar</strong></a>. Feel free to <a href="/contact">reach out</a> if you'd like to collaborate!
    </p>
  </section>

  <!-- Research Preview -->
  <section class="home-section-preview">
    <h2>
      Featured Research
      <span style="font-size: 0.95rem; font-weight: normal; float: right; margin-top: 0.4rem;">
        <a href="/research">[All Research &amp; Papers &rarr;]</a>
      </span>
    </h2>

    <ul class="editorial-list">
      <li class="editorial-item">
        <h3 class="item-title">
          <a href="/research">A Unified Multimodal Framework for Fake News Detection Using BERT and Vision Transformers</a>
          <span class="badge badge-green">Accepted &amp; Presented</span>
          <span class="badge">96.66% SOTA Acc</span>
        </h3>
        <div class="item-meta">
          <strong>Ayush Mishra</strong> et al. • <em>International Conference on Intelligent Computing, Cognitive Networks, and Smart Systems (IC2NS2)</em> • <strong>Accepted &amp; Presented (Tentative Publication: Dec 2026)</strong> • IEEE / Springer
        </div>
        <p class="item-desc">
          Pioneered an end-to-end multimodal architecture combining disentangled contextual language representations (DeBERTa-v3 / RoBERTa / BERT) and visual feature hierarchies (Swin Transformer, CLIP-ViT). Introduced an adaptive <strong>Cross-Modal Gated Fusion layer</strong> that dynamically balances text and visual cues.
        </p>
        <div class="item-links">
          <a href="https://github.com/ayush190511" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">[Code on GitHub]</a>
          <button class="action-btn-link copy-bibtex-btn" data-paper="ic2ns2_2026">[BibTeX Citation]</button>
          <button class="action-btn-link open-arch-modal-btn">[Architecture Deep-Dive ↗]</button>
        </div>
      </li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <!-- Projects Preview -->
  <section class="home-section-preview">
    <h2>
      Featured Systems
      <span style="font-size: 0.95rem; font-weight: normal; float: right; margin-top: 0.4rem;">
        <a href="/projects">[All Projects &amp; Systems &rarr;]</a>
      </span>
    </h2>

    <ul class="editorial-list">
      <li class="editorial-item">
        <h3 class="item-title">
          <a href="/projects#disease-pipeline">End-to-End MLOps Disease Classification Pipeline</a>
          <span class="badge">96.55% CV Acc</span>
        </h3>
        <div class="item-meta">MLOps • Containerization • CI/CD • AWS</div>
        <p class="item-desc">
          Production-ready automated image classification system featuring dataset versioning with <strong>DVC</strong>, experiment logging with <strong>MLflow</strong>, containerization with <strong>Docker</strong>, and automated deployment to AWS EC2 via <strong>GitHub Actions</strong>.
        </p>
        <div class="item-links">
          <a href="https://github.com/ayush190511" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">[Pipeline Source Code]</a>
        </div>
      </li>

      <li class="editorial-item">
        <h3 class="item-title">
          <a href="/projects#churn-engine">Real-Time Customer Churn &amp; Score Prediction Engine</a>
          <span class="badge">&lt;50ms Latency</span>
        </h3>
        <div class="item-meta">Machine Learning • Explainable AI • FastAPI</div>
        <p class="item-desc">
          High-throughput ML inference engine benchmarking 8 ensemble models (XGBoost, CatBoost, GradientBoost). Provides local and global model explainability via <strong>SHAP</strong>, RESTful microservices via <strong>FastAPI</strong>, and interactive dashboards via <strong>Streamlit</strong>.
        </p>
        <div class="item-links">
          <a href="https://github.com/ayush190511" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">[Source &amp; Explainability]</a>
        </div>
      </li>
    </ul>
  </section>
</Layout>
